    "q-141487": {
      "dom_id": "step-q141487",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Let $T:{R}^{7}\\to {R}^{7}$ be a linear transformation whose standard matrix is $T.$ Consider the following statement:\n\n*If $T({v}_{1})=T({v}_{2})$ if and only if ${v}_{1}={v}_{2},$  then $\\text{__________}.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne \\{0\\}$\n\nII. $T$ is a bijection\n\nIII. $\\text{rank}(T)=7$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $T$ is a linear transformation from ${R}^{7}$ into ${R}^{7},$ the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n $T$ is a bijection (an invertible transformation) $\\,⟺\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Im}(T)={R}^{7} \\\\  & \\text{rank}(T)=7 \\\\  & \\text{Ker}(T)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{nullity}(T)=0\\end{aligned}$\n\nSince $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\nT({v}_{1})=T({v}_{2})\\,⟹\\,T({v}_{1}-{v}_{2})=0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $T({v}_{1})=T({v}_{2})$ if and only if ${v}_{1}={v}_{2},$ we must have that $\\text{Ker}(T)=\\{0\\}.$\n\n- Statement II is true. According to the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{Ker}(T)=\\{0\\},$ the transformation $T$ is a bijection.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $T$ is a bijection, the invertible matrix theorem implies that $\\text{rank}(T)=7.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
